<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:40:04 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>科学家从世界上最古老的乌龟身上取出了脸颊拭子。他的DNA可能揭示长寿的线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-took-a-cheek-swab-from-the-worlds-oldest-tortoise-his-dna-could-reveal-hints-to-longevity-180989663/</link><description>乔纳森是一只亚达伯拉象龟，大约 194 岁，是当今现存最古老的陆地动物。关于他的遗传学的发现可以为延长人类寿命提供线索</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:28:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-took-a-cheek-swab-from-the-worlds-oldest-tortoise-his-dna-could-reveal-hints-to-longevity-180989663/</guid></item><item><title>这枚独一无二的青铜戒指让人一睹亚历山大灯塔的风采，这是古代世界失落的奇迹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-one-of-a-kind-bronze-ring-offers-a-tantalizing-glimpse-at-the-lighthouse-of-alexandria-a-lost-wonder-of-the-ancient-world-180989661/</link><description>埃及考古学家在安蒂罗多斯岛进行挖掘时发现了图章戒指，该岛曾经拥有一座奢华的托勒密宫殿</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:21:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-one-of-a-kind-bronze-ring-offers-a-tantalizing-glimpse-at-the-lighthouse-of-alexandria-a-lost-wonder-of-the-ancient-world-180989661/</guid></item><item><title>一个世纪前，在建造狮身人面像的岩石中发现了一个已灭绝的鳄鱼头骨。事实证明，它属于一个新物种</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-century-ago-an-extinct-crocidilians-skull-was-found-in-the-rocks-that-built-the-sphinx-turns-out-it-belonged-to-a-new-species-180989641/</link><description>根据一项新的研究，该标本长期以来被贴错标签。古生物学家将其鉴定为一种此前未被描述过的鳄类属和种——鳄鱼和短吻鳄的近亲——他们以古埃及神荷鲁斯的名字命名。</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-century-ago-an-extinct-crocidilians-skull-was-found-in-the-rocks-that-built-the-sphinx-turns-out-it-belonged-to-a-new-species-180989641/</guid></item><item><title>9月份的臭氧空洞是25年来最大的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/septembers-ozone-hole-was-the-biggest-it-has-been-in-25-years-180989657/</link><description>平流层臭氧层空洞的大小每年都会发生变化，但上个月的空洞面积特别大，达到 1060 万平方英里。</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:55:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/septembers-ozone-hole-was-the-biggest-it-has-been-in-25-years-180989657/</guid></item><item><title>由社区主导的苏格兰小岛上的考古发掘出土了一座具有“国际重要性”的中世纪修道院</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-community-led-archaeology-dig-on-a-tiny-scottish-isle-has-unearthed-a-medieval-monastery-of-international-importance-180989654/</link><description>该定居点由一位早期基督教圣人在 500 年代建立，“远远不仅仅是一座小岛上的教堂”。它在英国基督教化过程中发挥的作用可能比历史学家曾经意识到的更大</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:35:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-community-led-archaeology-dig-on-a-tiny-scottish-isle-has-unearthed-a-medieval-monastery-of-international-importance-180989654/</guid></item><item><title>这些南美鸟类的声音可与手提钻震耳欲聋的声音相媲美，使它们成为世界上已知最响亮的鸟类之一</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-south-american-birds-can-match-a-jackhammers-ear-splitting-volume-making-them-some-of-the-worlds-loudest-known-avians-180989629/</link><description>裸喉钟鸟和红腿鸫可以发出超过 120 分贝的声音，这使它们与吹喇叭的大象或电锯相当</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-south-american-birds-can-match-a-jackhammers-ear-splitting-volume-making-them-some-of-the-worlds-loudest-known-avians-180989629/</guid></item><item><title>德国考古学家在森林地面以下几英寸处出土了一座可能供奉战神火星的罗马神庙</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/just-inches-below-the-forest-floor-archaeologists-in-germany-unearthed-a-roman-temple-likely-dedicated-to-mars-the-god-of-war-180989650/</link><description>研究人员在卡珀斯堡堡垒附近挖掘时发现了该建筑的遗迹以及雕像碎片，卡珀斯堡堡垒是位于现代法兰克福郊区的古罗马军事防御工事</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 19:32:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/just-inches-below-the-forest-floor-archaeologists-in-germany-unearthed-a-roman-temple-likely-dedicated-to-mars-the-god-of-war-180989650/</guid></item><item><title>JMW 特纳 (JMW Turner) 在近 200 年前绘制了这幅令人惊叹的罗马风景画。如果你仔细看，你还能看到他的指纹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/jmw-turner-painted-this-breathtaking-roman-landscape-nearly-200-years-ago-if-you-look-closely-you-can-still-see-his-fingerprints-180989659/</link><description>这位浪漫主义画家于1830年代完成了《罗马，来自阿文丁山》。这件作品成为他 2014 年最昂贵的艺术品，预计 12 月的售价将再创纪录</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:56:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/jmw-turner-painted-this-breathtaking-roman-landscape-nearly-200-years-ago-if-you-look-closely-you-can-still-see-his-fingerprints-180989659/</guid></item><item><title>使人类首次登月成为可能的软件工程师先驱玛格丽特·汉密尔顿 (Margaret Hamilton) 去世，享年 90 岁</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/margaret-hamilton-a-pioneering-software-engineer-who-made-the-first-human-moon-landing-possible-dies-at-90-180989653/</link><description>汉密尔顿普及了“软件工程师”一词，并创建了可以预测问题的计算机程序。她获得了总统自由勋章并入选国家航空名人堂</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:42:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/margaret-hamilton-a-pioneering-software-engineer-who-made-the-first-human-moon-landing-possible-dies-at-90-180989653/</guid></item><item><title>加拿大诗人安妮·卡森将古代智慧带给现代观众。现在，她是诺贝尔文学奖获得者</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/canadian-poet-anne-carson-brings-ancient-wisdom-to-modern-audiences-now-shes-a-nobel-laureate-in-literature-180989655/</link><description>这位 76 岁的诗人、翻译家和散文家以其“大胆而富有创意”的方式将诗歌、散文及其之间的一切融为一体，从而形成了瑞典学院所说的“当代文学的新形式”。</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:23:30 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/canadian-poet-anne-carson-brings-ancient-wisdom-to-modern-audiences-now-shes-a-nobel-laureate-in-literature-180989655/</guid></item><item><title>美国部分地区的流感季节提前开始，专家表示您应该考虑尽快接种季节性疫苗。以下是您需要了解的内容</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/flu-season-started-early-in-parts-of-the-us-and-experts-say-you-should-consider-getting-the-seasonal-jab-asap-heres-what-to-know-180989639/</link><description>该季节通常从十月或十一月开始。但包括加利福尼亚州、华盛顿州、阿拉斯加和夏威夷在内的一些西部州早在八月份就开始出现流感病例上升的情况</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 15:24:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/flu-season-started-early-in-parts-of-the-us-and-experts-say-you-should-consider-getting-the-seasonal-jab-asap-heres-what-to-know-180989639/</guid></item><item><title>窃贼在法国又实施了一起令人震惊的艺术品抢劫案。这次，他们拿走了萨尔瓦多·达利设计的 330 磅重的青铜书籍封面</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thieves-pulled-off-another-shocking-art-heist-in-france-this-time-they-took-a-330-pound-bronze-book-cover-designed-by-salvador-dali-180989638/</link><description>《启示录书》是​​ 14 位艺术家和作家合作的“杰作”。这是有史以来最重、最昂贵的书之一</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thieves-pulled-off-another-shocking-art-heist-in-france-this-time-they-took-a-330-pound-bronze-book-cover-designed-by-salvador-dali-180989638/</guid></item><item><title>非洲象经常发出低沉的隆隆声。现在，科学家们正在使用人工智能来解码联合发声</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/african-elephants-often-produce-choruses-of-low-pitched-rumbles-now-scientists-are-using-ai-to-decode-the-joint-vocalizations-180989620/</link><description>新的研究表明，动物的重叠叫声可以作为协调的群体信息，并且可能包含个体隆隆声中编码之外的其他信息</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/african-elephants-often-produce-choruses-of-low-pitched-rumbles-now-scientists-are-using-ai-to-decode-the-joint-vocalizations-180989620/</guid></item><item><title>数百名英国大学生在 1966 年黑斯廷斯战役的重演中用木剑发生冲突。观看重新发现的丢失镜头的“时间胶囊”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hundreds-of-british-college-students-clashed-with-wooden-swords-in-a-1966-re-enactment-of-the-battle-of-hastings-watch-the-rediscovered-time-capsule-of-lost-footage-180989635/</link><description>一名当地摄影师在重演过程中拍摄了 300 卷彩色胶片，其中显示了“步行的士兵与马匹的距离非常接近”以及“对健康和安全的相当轻松的态度”。该活动引发了一项持续至今的年度传统</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hundreds-of-british-college-students-clashed-with-wooden-swords-in-a-1966-re-enactment-of-the-battle-of-hastings-watch-the-rediscovered-time-capsule-of-lost-footage-180989635/</guid></item><item><title>两位化学家因揭开分子“手性”之谜、帮助制药商开发更安全的药物而获得诺贝尔奖</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-chemists-win-nobel-prize-for-unraveling-a-mystery-of-molecular-handedness-helping-drugmakers-develop-safer-medications-180989643/</link><description>许多分子有两种镜像形式——就像左手和右手——但生物体通常只包含一种。然而，化学家无法弄清楚如何在实验室中只制造一种版本。 Henri Kagan 和 Kenso Soai 因解决难题而分享奖项</description><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:10:13 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-chemists-win-nobel-prize-for-unraveling-a-mystery-of-molecular-handedness-helping-drugmakers-develop-safer-medications-180989643/</guid></item><item><title>斯坦利·库布里克的个人档案即将拍卖，其中包括《闪灵》中的斧头和《2001：太空漫游》中的星童</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stanley-kubricks-personal-archive-is-going-up-for-auction-including-the-ax-from-the-shining-and-the-star-child-from-2001-a-space-odyssey-180989632/</link><description>传奇导演的现场椅子、注释剧本和道具让您一睹《全金属外壳》和《大开眼戒》等电影背后细致的电影制作过程</description><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 17:48:09 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stanley-kubricks-personal-archive-is-going-up-for-auction-including-the-ax-from-the-shining-and-the-star-child-from-2001-a-space-odyssey-180989632/</guid></item><item><title>研究人员可能首次直接观测到系外行星的磁场，为更深入地观察遥远世界带来了希望</title